dor Suspension Policy","content":"Vendor accounts may be suspended by procurement managers or compliance officers when there is documented evidence of policy breach. Suspension halts all new purchase orders and invoice submissions. Active invoices remain payable. Suspension requires a written justification logged in the audit trail. Reinstatement requires compliance officer approval.","sensitivity":"restricted","allowed_roles":["procurement_manager","compliance_officer"],"score":0.2912,"tags":["vendor","suspend","compliance","procurement"],"tenant":"acme","source":"system","version_hash":"abcdef1234567890","timestamp_indexed":"2026-09-18T09:56:22.196548+00:00","is_untrusted_user_content":false},{"doc_id":"POL-006","title":"Prohibited Operations Policy","content":"The following operations are prohibited for all actors via automated agent requests: modifying audit trail records, deleting data from the vendor_invoices table (tombstoning via ARCHIVED status is permitted instead), granting system-level access, and executing raw SQL queries. Any request that attempts to perform a prohibited operation must be blocked and escalated to a security officer.","sensitivity":"public","allowed_roles":[],"score":0.2497,"tags":["prohibited","security","audit","delete","block"],"tenant":"acme","source":"system","version_hash":"abcdef1234567890","timestamp_indexed":"2026-09-18T09:56:22.196548+00:00","is_untrusted_user_content":false}],"retrieval_note":"NiyamEvidence — ACL-filtered retriever + deterministic NLI (Week 5)"}}
